WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.580
You need four gallon zip bags, about two cups of vegetable shortening, tape, and a

2
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.580
bowl of ice water.

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.060
Make two mittens from pairs of bags.

4
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.160
Put shortening between one pair, and nothing between the other.

5
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.020
Tape the tops. Then dip both into ice water, up to the wrist.

6
00:00:18.783 --> 00:00:22.123
The plain mitten hand usually feels cold well before the other one.

7
00:00:22.703 --> 00:00:23.703
Your times will vary.

8
00:00:24.303 --> 00:00:27.363
The fat slows the heat leaving, as blubber does for a seal.

9
00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:32.287
Stay with your child the whole time, and never leave the bowl of water alone.

10
00:00:32.987 --> 00:00:37.327
Every try stops at one minute, and your child can pull a hand out any time.

11
00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:39.487
Stop at once if a hand hurts.
